LOK: Impress charts, notes and comments without dialogs

- .uno:InsertObjectChart takes Chart (look and data as JSON): it inserts
  a chart at the slide centre with no chart UI, or, with one chart
  marked, changes that chart on a copy that replaces it (one undo step).
  A look or table that does not parse is refused. The look goes in
  before the data, so the data sees the chart's type.
- .uno:Chart reads the marked chart's name, look and data.
- .uno:SlideNotes (new) sets slide Part's notes as plain text in one
  undo step. Text with one look throughout, paragraph and character
  (PowerPoint sets the full look on every run), keeps it; text whose
  look varies is refused, as plain text would lose it. Its read gives
  the shown slide's index, the text and whether the look varies
  ("rich").
- Comments read with their slide's index.
- A new comment or reply takes the user's name when the view has no
  author (a kit client sets the name with setOption("author")); it was
  left blank.

